INT. ROOFTOP GREENHOUSE, APARTMENT BLOCK - DAWN

Tomato cages, herb pots, a rusted bistro table. The city wakes in haze below.

PHILOMENA ADEBAYO-STRAND (60s, cardigan, trowel) waters basil. Across from her, her son NIKOLAI (30s, borrowed suit, unslept) cradles a mug.

She waters. He sips. Neither looks.

PHILOMENA
You came early.

NIKOLAI
Train was on time.

PHILOMENA
First time in years.

He nods. She moves to the tomatoes. He follows with his eyes.

NIKOLAI
It looks good up here.

PHILOMENA
Your father built the cages.

NIKOLAI
I remember.

PHILOMENA
He'd have hated the basil.

NIKOLAI
He hated everything green.

They share a quiet smile. It lingers.

PHILOMENA
Nik.

NIKOLAI
Mm.

He sets down the mug. She sets down the can. They look at each other for the first time.

NIKOLAI
I'm sorry I wasn't here.

^PHILOMENA
I sold the house.

A pause. Neither moves. The basil drips.

NIKOLAI
You what?

PHILOMENA
It's done. Papers signed Friday.

Nikolai picks up the mug. Sets it down. Picks it up again. She watches his hands. Behind them, the sun clears the rooftops.
